# Bulk Action Implementation Patterns

## Standard Bulk Action Structure

### 1. Data Normalization ⚠️
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT Pattern - Always normalize IDs
const normalizedData = useMemo(() => {
  return data.map(item => ({
    ...item,
    id: item.entity_id // Normalize ID field for selection
  }));
}, [data]);

// 🚫 WRONG - Using raw data without normalization
const data = items.map(item => item); // Missing ID normalization
```

### 2. Bulk Action Handler Pattern
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT Implementation
const handleBulkAction = async (action, selectedIds) => {
  try {
    // Convert normalized IDs back to entity IDs
    const entityIds = selectedIds.map(id => {
      const entity = entities.find(e => e.id === id);
      return entity.entity_id;
    });

    const payload = {
      user_id: adminData.user_id,
      action: action,
      app_source: "pos_app",
      entity_ids: entityIds
    };

    await bulkAction.mutateAsync(payload);
    setSelectedItems([]);
    toastController.success('Bulk action completed successfully!');
  } catch (error) {
    toastController.error(error.response?.data?.detail || 'Failed to process bulk action');
  }
};
```

### 3. API Integration Pattern
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT Pattern in hooks file
const bulkAction = useMutation({
  mutationFn: async (payload) => {
    const response = await axios.post(
      'https://men4u.xyz/v2/common/bulk_entity_action',
      payload,
      {
        headers: {
          Authorization: getToken()  // ✅ CORRECT: getToken() includes Bearer
        }
      }
    );
    return response.data;
  },
  onSuccess: () => {
    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.entity.list() });
    refetch(); // Explicitly refetch to ensure latest data
  }
});
```

## DataTable Integration

### 1. Component Setup
```javascript
<DataTable
  data={normalizedData}
  enableSelection={true}
  onSelectionChange={setSelectedItems}
  selectedItems={selectedItems}
  onBulkAction={handleBulkAction}
  idField="id"  // Use normalized id field
/>
```

### 2. Selection State Management
```javascript
const [selectedItems, setSelectedItems] = useState([]);
// Reset selection after successful bulk action
setSelectedItems([]);
```

## Best Practices

### 1. ID Handling
- Always normalize IDs for consistent selection
- Convert back to entity IDs when making API calls
- Use proper type conversion if needed (parseInt, etc.)

### 2. Error Handling
- Implement proper error handling
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log errors for debugging

### 3. State Management
- Reset selection after successful action
- Update UI immediately after action
- Handle loading states

### 4. API Payload
- Follow consistent payload structure
- Include required metadata (user_id, app_source)
- Validate IDs before sending

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

1. ⚠️ ID Mismatch
   - Always verify ID mapping
   - Ensure proper type conversion
   - Validate ID existence

2. ⚠️ State Inconsistency
   - Reset selection after action
   - Update cache properly
   - Handle partial success/failure

3. ⚠️ Error Handling
   - Handle network errors
   - Show user feedback
   - Maintain data consistency

